===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|dance}} Of or relating to [[dancing]].
#* {{RQ:Thackeray Pendennis||passage=The pair danced away with great agility and contentment,—first a waltz, then a galop, then a waltz again, until, in the second waltz, they were bumped by another couple who had joined the '''Terpsichorean''' choir.|47}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1865|author=Charles Dickens|title=Our Mutual Friend|passage=This was such an entirely new view of the '''Terpsichorean''' art as socially practised, that Mrs Lammle looked at her young friend in some astonishment}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1939|author=T. S. Eliot|chapter=The Song of the Jellicles|title=Old Possum's Book of Practical Cats
|passage=They're quiet enough in the morning hours,<br>They're quiet enough in the afternoon,<br>Reserving their '''terpsichorean''' powers<br>To dance by the light of the Jellicle Moon.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1970|author=Monty Python|title=The Cheese Shop|passage=Oh, heaven forbid: I am one who delights in all manifestations of the '''Terpsichorean''' muse!}}

